---
Implement chorus effect (modulated delay for thickening).

Classic chorus using a short modulated delay line. Two voices with
LFO-modulated delay times create a thicker, wider sound.

## Parameters
- rate: LFO speed (0.1-10 Hz, default 1.5)
- depth: Modulation depth in ms (0-10ms, default 3.0)
- wet: Wet/dry mix (0-1, default 0.5)
- voices: Number of chorus voices (1-4, default 2)

## Implementation
- Short delay buffer (~50ms max)
- Per-voice LFO with phase offset (120° apart for 3 voices)
- Linear interpolation for fractional delay reads
- Stereo spread: voices panned L/R

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] EFFECT_CHORUS added to effect type enum
- [ ] Smooth modulation with no zipper noise
- [ ] Works in effect chain (per-track and master)
- [ ] Parameters exposed in mixer view

## Test Plan
- [ ] Verify chorus thickens a simple sine wave
- [ ] Verify no clicks/pops during parameter changes
- [ ] ASan: no buffer overflows with extreme depth values
